WEBVTT

00:04:27.748 --> 00:04:30.328
and I poked my head
through a colleague's door.

00:04:30.352 --> 00:04:33.494
"Dude, there's gotta be a better way."

00:04:34.122 --> 00:04:37.059
He asked if I had heard
of this new technology called LiDAR --

00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:38.537
Light Detection And Ranging.

00:04:38.561 --> 00:04:39.926
I looked it up.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:43.293
LiDAR involves shooting
a dense grid of laser pulses

00:04:43.317 --> 00:04:46.122
from an airplane to the ground's surface.

00:04:46.146 --> 00:04:49.090
What you end up with
is a high-resolution scan

00:04:49.114 --> 00:04:51.238
of the earth's surface
and everything on it.

00:04:51.712 --> 00:04:53.214
It's not an image,

00:04:53.238 --> 00:04:56.662
but instead it's a dense,
three-dimensional plot of points.

00:04:57.236 --> 00:04:59.541
We had enough money in the scan,

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.327
so we did just that.